SUMMARY:Uncomputable Thread
LOCATION:Mass MoCA\, 1040 Mass MoCA Way\, North Adams\, MA 01247
DESCRIPTION:Presentation and Movement Workshop\nUncomputable Thread is a pr
 esentation\, conversation and participatory movement workshop by artist Ta
 eyoon Choi\, created in collaboration with scholar Alexander R. Galloway\,
  choreographer Cori Kresge and artist Roopa Vasudevan. The work examines t
 he history of textile in relation to computing\, alongside the artistic an
 d political significance of what cannot be computed and draws on themes of
  the current exhibition\, Technologies of Relation\, which includes works 
 by both Choi and Vasudevan.\nhttps://massmoca.org/event/uncomputable-threa
 d-a-technologies-of-relation-lecture-performance/\nFrom Pushpin Western Ma
 ss: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://massmoca.org/event/uncomputable-thread-a-technologies-of-relati
 on-lecture-performance/
END:VEVENT
