SUMMARY:Endea Owens & The Cookout
LOCATION:Mass MoCA\, 1040 Mass MoCA Way\, North Adams\, MA 01247
DESCRIPTION:Known as one of jazz’s most vibrant emerging artists\, Endea 
 Owens is a Detroit-raised recording artist\, bassist\, and composer. She h
 as been mentored by jazz icons the likes of Marcus Belgrave\, Rodney Whita
 ker\, and Ron Carter. She has toured and performed with Wynton Marsalis\, 
 Jennifer Holliday\, Diana Ross\, Rhonda Ross\, Solange\, Jon Batiste\, Jaz
 zmeia Horn\, Dee Dee Bridgewater\, and Cyrus Chestnut\, to name a few.\nht
 tps://massmoca.org/event/endea-owens-the-cookout/\nFrom Pushpin Western Ma
 ss: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://massmoca.org/event/endea-owens-the-cookout/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1c7495b454698d22e4f3714b030ee6f3629def0d@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261118T220000Z
DTEND:20261119T000000Z
SUMMARY:On the Calculation of Volume (Book I) by Solvej Balle
LOCATION:Mass MoCA\, 1040 Mass MoCA Way\, North Adams\, MA 01247
DESCRIPTION:Book Talk with Lizzie Whitman\n“How on earth did this book co
 me into being? It’s like it has always been here in this world with us\,
  like one feels about the best art. I am torn as I read it between lingeri
 ng and racing ahead\, and I think about my days completely differently now
 .” — Sheila Heti Lizzie Whitman convenes this casual book club around 
 Solvej Balle’s utterly riveting On the Calculation of Volume (Book I) 
 — the grand opening of her speculative fiction septology\, winner of the
  2022 Nordic Council Literature Prize (Scandinavia’s most important lite
 rary award) for being “a masterpiece of its time.” Balle was also nomi
 nated for the International Booker Prize and a National Book Award for thi
 s book.\nhttps://massmoca.org/event/lizzie-whitman-on-on-the-calculation-o
 f-volume-book-i/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernm
 a/
URL:https://massmoca.org/event/lizzie-whitman-on-on-the-calculation-of-volu
 me-book-i/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b478b7c140927a9a3c9d233b63f54a89c0ec3b4d@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261121T220000Z
DTEND:20261122T000000Z
SUMMARY:Last Week in End Times Cinema & Algorithm of the Night
LOCATION:Mass MoCA\, 1040 Mass MoCA Way\, North Adams\, MA 01247
DESCRIPTION:A.S. Hamrah\n“A. S. Hamrah’s writing on film is a delight..
 . Like all the best criticism\, his writing makes art and life feel less l
 onely.” —Elif Batuman A.S. Hamrah is single-handedly re-inventing film
  criticism with a unique archive of unfortunate movie bulletins published 
 in the best indie print journals and magazines\, and compiled for his belo
 ved weekly newsletter. His two most recent books\, Last Week in End Times 
 Cinema (Semiotext(e)) and Algorithm of the Night (n+1) are R&D Store best-
 sellers. Join Hamrah for a conversation about film\, filmmakers\, critical
  writing\, and the state of movies in 2026.\nhttps://massmoca.org/event/a-
 s-hamrah-last-week-in-end-times-cinema/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https:
 //pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://massmoca.org/event/a-s-hamrah-last-week-in-end-times-cinema/
END:VEVENT
